meta {
  name: Sign In (Browser)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{auth_url}}/.well-known/openid-configuration
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

script:post-response {
  // `auth: inherit` runs the collection's OAuth2 config (authorization code + PKCE): with no
  // cached token, Bruno opens a browser window on the real /signin page, catches the callback
  // on :8090 and exchanges the code. Export what it got so {{access_token}} works anywhere.
  const authorization = req.getHeader('Authorization') || '';
  const jwt = authorization.replace(/^Bearer /, '');
  if (!jwt) {
    console.log('no token — the sign-in window was closed or the dance failed; run again');
    return;
  }
  bru.setEnvVar('access_token', jwt);

  const decode = (part) => {
    const b64 = part.replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/');
    return JSON.parse(Buffer.from(b64.padEnd(Math.ceil(b64.length / 4) * 4, '='), 'base64').toString());
  };
  const claims = decode(jwt.split('.')[1]);
  console.log('signed in as:', claims.sub, claims.email || '', JSON.stringify(claims.role || ''));
  console.log('expires:', new Date(claims.exp * 1000).toISOString(), '(auto-refreshed by Bruno)');

  // Newer Bruno versions expose the stored OAuth2 credentials to scripts; export the refresh
  // token too when this one does.
  try {
    if (typeof bru.getOauth2CredentialVar === 'function') {
      const refresh = bru.getOauth2CredentialVar('$oauth2.credentials.refresh_token');
      if (refresh) bru.setEnvVar('refresh_token', refresh);
    }
  } catch (ignored) {}
}

docs {
  The front door: run this to sign in through the real browser flow and come back holding tokens.

  What happens: Bruno opens a window on auth's own sign-in page (the same page every real client
  sees), you sign in, auth redirects to Bruno's callback with a code, Bruno exchanges it — PKCE,
  no client secret — then this script stashes the access token in the `access_token` env var and
  logs the claims to the console drawer. Every request with `auth: inherit` uses the cached token
  automatically (and refreshes it); `{{access_token}}` is for anything else.

  Registering a new account, entirely in the browser: the sign-in window links to
  "Create an account". Register there (or at http://localhost:5100/register), open Mailpit at
  http://localhost:8025, click the emailed link, press Confirm — then run this request again and
  sign in with the new credentials.

  Switching users: clear the cached token in the collection's Auth settings first, or Bruno will
  keep using the one it has. If the window then signs you straight back in without showing the
  form, its cookie session is still alive — close and reopen Bruno to drop it (the sign-out
  story lands with the end-session work in the design/finalize pass).
}
